    "text": "David Vollrath, 1st District Commissioner | Berrien County\nDavid Vollrath, 1st District Commissioner | Berrien County\nHeavy snowfall and strong winds on November 28 led to about three inches of wet snow accumulating in the park, resulting in several downed trees across trails. The ground remains unfrozen, and trail clearing efforts are ongoing.\nPark officials have requested that hikers and dog walkers avoid using the trails until further notice. Snowshoe rentals will be available today for use on designated trails only.\n\"We will update when there is enough snow and trails are clear to start grooming,\" officials stated. \"We are looking forward to a great ski season!\"\nTrail users are advised to monitor updates regarding trail conditions and grooming schedules.",
